<!-- Build template. Terminology: application programming interface (API); command-line interface (CLI); Verifier Standard (VSTD). -->
<div class="home-intro"><div class="eyebrow">VERIFIER STANDARD · VERSION 2.0.0 CANDIDATE SOURCE</div>
<h1>Make computational claims<br><em>checkable.</em></h1>
<p class="home-lead">Capture a computation. Bind its artifacts to a precise claim. Give someone else a bounded way to inspect, reproduce, or refute it.</p>
<p class="home-description">Verifier is the Python reference implementation of the Verifier Standard (VSTD), a verification-domain language for portable, bounded, refutable evidence about computational claims. These pages describe unreleased v2.0.0 candidate source; the published 1.5.0 package has a separate archive.</p>
<div class="home-actions"><a class="portal-button primary" href="@/docs/INSTALLATION.html">Start with v2 source <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="portal-button" href="@/reference.html#api">Explore the v2 Python reference</a></div></div>
<section id="start-building" class="start-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">FROM V2 SOURCE TO FIRST CHECK</span><h2>A small place to start.</h2><p>Use the v2 candidate checkout identified by this site's source coordinate. Install it locally, then run the defensive demo before capturing your own computation.</p><a href="@/docs/FIRST_RECEIPT.html">Follow the receipt walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-top"><span class="terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span> Terminal <span>Python 3.10+</span></div><pre><code># In the v2.0.0 candidate source checkout
python -m pip install .
vstd demo
vstd --help</code></pre><div class="terminal-foot">Distribution: verifier-standard · Import: verifier · Command: vstd</div></div></section>
<section id="explore" class="explore-section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Find your path</h2><span>Learn → inspect → contribute</span></div><div class="portal-cards">
